# Building on Flynet

Build on Flynet through the published SDK — never hand-roll `fetch()` or invent endpoints.

- `@flynetdev/core` — framework-agnostic TypeScript client (two clients, OAuth, typed errors, money + pagination helpers).
- `@flynetdev/react` — `FlynetProvider` + TanStack hooks + themeable components, built on core.

## Two credentials, two route families (the #1 mistake)

The API has two auth schemes; they are NOT interchangeable.

- `X-API-Key` → Discovery routes (`/restaurants*`, `/locations*`). Server-only.
- `Authorization: Bearer <JWT>` → member routes (`/users/me/*`, `/check_ins*`, `/memberships`, `/payment_intents*`).

`@flynetdev/core` enforces this with two clients:

```ts
const discovery = new FlynetDiscoveryClient({ apiKey: process.env.API_KEY! }); // server-only
const member = new FlynetMemberClient({ accessToken });                        // OAuth JWT
```

## Rules to honor

1. Use the right header for the route family (rule above).
2. `/users/me/*` is canonical — there is no `/users/{id}/*` form (it 404s).
3. PKCE is required on `/oauth/authorize`; token exchange needs `client_secret` AND `code_verifier`. Use `FlynetOAuth` / `createPkcePair`.
4. OAuth 401s have an empty body — the cause is in `WWW-Authenticate`.
5. Wrong scope → 403 `insufficient_scope`, not 404. Scopes: `read:profile`, `read:checkins`, `read:wallets`.
6. Unknown filter params are silently ignored — filter client-side if the server behavior isn't shipped.
7. No payment webhooks in v1 — poll `GET /payment_intents/{id}`.
8. `payment0030` = insufficient FLY on confirm — pre-check `GET /users/me/wallets`.

Catch errors as `FlynetError` and branch on `error.kind` / `error.code`, not raw HTTP. Format money with `formatFly` (18-decimal wei) / `formatUsdCents` (integer cents).

## React

Wrap the tree in `FlynetProvider` (it owns the TanStack `QueryClient` — never construct your own); pass constructed clients (`member` / `discovery`). Compose the real components: `WalletBadge`, `CheckInFeed`, `RestaurantList`, `RestaurantCard`, `LocationCard`, `OpenHoursBadge`, `NearbyLocations`, `UserPassport`, `RecentVisits`, `ConnectWithBlackbird`. Do NOT reference Pay-with-FLY, Tags Strip / TagGate, Payment Receipt, or Location Map — they are not built.

## Never

- Put `API_KEY` or `client_secret` in browser code.
- Use `/users/{id}/*` paths, expect JSON on OAuth 401s, or expect payment webhooks.
- Invent fields, endpoints, or components not in the OpenAPI spec.
